  "reply_to_user": "Hi Dana, thanks for reporting this. I checked your laptop (BL-LT-0101) remotely and it looks healthy: about 310 GB of its 512 GB main drive is free (roughly 60%), and there are no storage warnings. That doesn't match the message you're seeing, so I need a bit more information before we do anything. Could you reply with: (1) the exact wording of the Windows message, or a screenshot, and which drive letter it names (for example C:, D:, or a USB or external drive), and (2) whether a USB stick, external drive, or SD card was plugged in when it appeared. If the warning is about an external or USB drive, emptying the Recycle Bin and clearing old files from that drive usually fixes it. If it's about your main drive, you can also go to Settings > System > Storage > Temporary files and remove them. Once I hear back, I'll take it from there.",
  "internal_note": "Sender is Dana Whitfield, CEO and a VIP. Followed KB-017 quick check. check_device_status on BL-LT-0101: online, last check-in 2026-10-11 03:16 UTC, 512 GB total, 310 GB free (60.5%), no warnings. That is well above the 10% threshold, so the reported low-disk warning doesn't match the main drive. Possible causes: an external, USB, or secondary drive, a stale or one-off warning, or the user is looking at a different device. No remote cleanup tool is available. Asked the user for the exact message or a screenshot, the drive letter, and whether any removable media was connected. If the main drive turns out to be affected after all and is still under 10% after cleanup, escalate per KB-017. Given VIP status, follow up promptly.",
